 "title": "3 Tips to Make Claude Motion Graphics Unique",
 "topic": "ai tools",
 "summary": "The creator shares three tips to make Claude motion graphics videos stand out from others. The advice covers using open-source projects to avoid building effects from scratch, maintaining context with workspaces, and generating custom music.",
 "key_points": [
  "Open-source projects: Paste a GitHub link into Claude instead of building every effect from scratch so it can pull in the real code.",
  "Context: Use a workspace instead of one-off chats so Claude knows past projects, brand details, and templates.",
  "Music: Use Suno to generate a custom track that matches the pace and mood of the edit."
 ],
 "content": "Three tips to separate your Claude videos from others. Number one, open-source projects. Don't build every effect from scratch. These are the few unique visuals I use. I paste in the repo link and say what to use, then Claude pulls in the actual code. Number two, context. I use a workspace instead of one-off chats. Claude can see my past projects and preferences, so I can say insert my best clips to my profile grid and this is what I get. Number three, music. Sound sets the pace and the mood. I use Suno which is an AI music generator so my agent can create a soundtrack on the fly that fits the video.",
